WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.495 --> 00:00:11.167
Hi, today, I'll be sharing an interesting topic,

00:00:11.168 --> 00:00:13.984
the 'extensible design for work life balance,'

00:00:13.985 --> 00:00:16.318
that I thought of coming to the platform.

00:00:16.855 --> 00:00:19.740
Before I start, let me introduce myself briefly

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:28.685
I'm Lee Jeong Eun, a web developer working at the e-commerce field

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:32.775
The next photo is something I took at JSConf EU

00:00:33.744 --> 00:00:37.183
I experienced it first at JSConfEU

00:00:37.184 --> 00:00:39.044
I could meet various people

00:00:39.287 --> 00:00:42.745
And had great memories, which led me to this spot

00:00:43.345 --> 00:00:46.485
It's my first time as a speaker, and I'm very nervous.

00:00:46.695 --> 00:00:50.415
But it's such an honor to be here at JSConf Korea and give a presentation

00:00:52.965 --> 00:00:56.723
So why did I think about extensible structure?

00:00:56.724 --> 00:00:58.465
What was it like before?

00:00:59.085 --> 00:01:00.704
What were the issues?

00:01:00.705 --> 00:01:02.595
And to resolve that

00:01:03.665 --> 00:01:05.129
What new extensible design is born?

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:08.955
And what benefits did I get from this changed structure?

00:01:11.115 --> 00:01:13.795
Why did we need a new design?

00:01:15.525 --> 00:01:17.634
Please look at this picture,

00:01:17.635 --> 00:01:19.815
What do you think this is?

00:01:21.476 --> 00:01:24.035
Can you add this spec within the schedule?

00:01:24.325 --> 00:01:27.205
Or, I want this function out for this occasion

00:01:27.385 --> 00:01:30.315
You hear that a lot at work

00:01:30.745 --> 00:01:33.895
I used to hear the same things a lot

00:01:34.045 --> 00:01:36.695
In order to respond to these changing needs

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.409
My code, unlike my intention,

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.544
could be overwhelming with layers of codes and exception handling

00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:45.815
Why is this the only way our project responds?

00:01:47.055 --> 00:01:49.305
Let's take a look at each

00:01:50.065 --> 00:01:54.705
First, the structure without considering scalability

00:01:56.165 --> 00:01:59.165
This was my original project structure

00:01:59.345 --> 00:02:02.431
The original one is something Dan Abramov introduced

00:02:02.432 --> 00:02:06.155
which is Presentational and Container pattern-based

00:02:06.715 --> 00:02:09.934
In the early service, the function wasn't too big

00:02:09.935 --> 00:02:14.385
The 1:1 component or communication structure didn't matter much

00:02:14.845 --> 00:02:20.255
As there were more functions and needs that we have to provide service for at the platform

00:02:20.256 --> 00:02:22.775
We faced various problems

00:02:25.405 --> 00:02:28.375
First, there was a structural problem in the overall flow

00:02:28.965 --> 00:02:33.361
The container component had all the business logics realized

00:02:33.362 --> 00:02:38.025
So without using the same container it was hard to reuse the logic

00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:41.673
When we needed the same function in the different UI

00:02:41.674 --> 00:02:44.809
We had to build another overlapping code in another container

00:02:46.725 --> 00:02:49.604
It's the same coupon receiving function

00:02:49.605 --> 00:02:51.401
But the modal provided at web

00:02:51.402 --> 00:02:54.955
And the page component at the in-app page divide

00:02:55.365 --> 00:02:56.235
Log-in

00:02:57.695 --> 00:02:58.855
Agreement check

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:02.485
And the actual download logic

00:03:02.486 --> 00:03:05.255
The same logic is written twice

00:03:06.135 --> 00:03:08.125
With more overlapping codes

00:03:09.576 --> 00:03:10.901
There were more uses

00:03:10.902 --> 00:03:15.185
So there were more human errors regarding missing a component here or there

00:03:16.065 --> 00:03:22.605
And the container component took charge of the most of the business logic

00:03:22.606 --> 00:03:26.726
So as the function got more complex, the component size grew

00:03:26.727 --> 00:03:28.945
And the code became hard to recognize

00:03:29.325 --> 00:03:32.570
With this growing problem

00:03:32.571 --> 00:03:35.555
We decided to reconfigure the project design

00:03:37.315 --> 00:03:39.525
How did we change the structure?

00:03:40.705 --> 00:03:43.815
Before the design we had to consider:

00:03:44.515 --> 00:03:47.072
We need to reuse the business logic

00:03:47.073 --> 00:03:51.546
The UI and business logic had to be combined with no connection

00:03:52.385 --> 00:03:54.855
And the duplicate code should be minimized

00:03:55.155 --> 00:03:58.404
DRY is one of the software development rules

00:03:58.405 --> 00:04:00.435
It stands for 'Don't Repeat Yourself'

00:04:02.085 --> 00:04:04.865
The next flow is the final structure

00:04:05.115 --> 00:04:08.865
It's layered differently from before

00:04:09.365 --> 00:04:13.087
Let me introduce one background for this design for context

00:04:13.088 --> 00:04:16.075
And show you this flow again later

00:04:16.745 --> 00:04:19.285
So let's go one by one

00:04:20.024 --> 00:04:22.096
For a smooth explanation

00:04:22.098 --> 00:04:27.055
Let's say that we are providing this video streaming service

00:04:30.605 --> 00:04:33.465
First we analyze the UI component

00:04:33.466 --> 00:04:37.918
Like this, at service, we can have UI aspects like logo, subscription button

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:40.735
Video, chatting, and more like that

00:04:41.285 --> 00:04:45.635
Even these separated aspects need a reusable structure

00:04:48.015 --> 00:04:50.202
Have you heard about an atomic design?

00:04:50.203 --> 00:04:52.455
If you have, raise your hand

00:04:52.635 --> 00:04:55.426
Many of you have

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:57.845
and I'm sure some of you haven't

00:04:58.175 --> 00:05:03.868
Atomic design, based on its name like atoms, molecules or organisms,

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:09.015
is a design system based on the organic structure that combines step by step

00:05:09.505 --> 00:05:13.172
Our focus was reusability

00:05:13.173 --> 00:05:16.098
So using that atomic design

00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:18.405
We took it as the UI component structure

00:05:20.657 --> 00:05:24.201
Going back to the example, you can use the smallest elements

00:05:24.747 --> 00:05:28.791
such as text, text buttons, icon buttons etc, as UI components,

00:05:29.252 --> 00:05:32.696
and you can combine these to create logo or chat next.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:38.531
You can further combine these to create chatting list or videos.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.239
And using all the above, you can create a page with UI.

00:05:45.212 --> 00:05:50.900
I wanted this UI components to be separate from business logic.

00:05:51.464 --> 00:05:55.463
If you use UI component that doesn't affect the server data,

00:05:56.052 --> 00:05:57.752
you can use the "storybook",

00:05:58.967 --> 00:06:00.948
and even without data,

00:06:02.346 --> 00:06:04.300
you can test your UI,

00:06:04.375 --> 00:06:07.315
and reduce the effect between UI and script development.

00:06:08.415 --> 00:06:10.572
Storybook can be published separately,

00:06:10.573 --> 00:06:15.573
and therefore, can show the final UI
without embodying the actual functions.

00:06:19.936 --> 00:06:24.411
To separate UI components from functions,

00:06:24.413 --> 00:06:28.155
now we created a fake component called feature component.

00:06:29.596 --> 00:06:32.998
You can accomplish actual functions in the feature component.

00:06:33.329 --> 00:06:36.693
The status admin library is a typical example of this.

00:06:38.657 --> 00:06:41.765
You can use this as a reference to UI components,

00:06:41.766 --> 00:06:44.600
now the server data isn't separated completely,

00:06:45.447 --> 00:06:49.258
so the UI component can only show

00:06:49.479 --> 00:06:52.935
what it can only express.

00:06:58.859 --> 00:07:02.000
Feature components are similar to

00:07:02.001 --> 00:07:04.611
container component that was previously mentioned.

00:07:05.266 --> 00:07:07.351
The difference is

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.816
the business logic is layered and separated.

00:07:12.272 --> 00:07:17.088
Going back to the example, say we want to create a subscribe function.

00:07:18.169 --> 00:07:21.380
The feature component has
an implementable subscribe,

00:07:21.676 --> 00:07:22.756
a subscribe function,

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:24.670
and you'll reference related data.

00:07:25.422 --> 00:07:28.633
Let's separate the layer for subscribe function.

00:07:34.177 --> 00:07:39.040
I named this layer "action layer" since it is user action based.

00:07:39.824 --> 00:07:42.822
If you consider the logic behind "subscribe" action wrapping,

00:07:43.264 --> 00:07:45.853
there's "subscribe" and "unsubscribe".

00:07:49.555 --> 00:07:53.023
What steps do you think we need to implement "subscribe"?

00:07:53.675 --> 00:07:56.973
I'll first have to check if I'm logged in.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.389
Based on the logged in user,

00:07:59.777 --> 00:08:02.046
you can either hit subscribe,

00:08:02.488 --> 00:08:05.211
or if you're not logged in, you can send them to login page,

00:08:05.212 --> 00:08:08.406
and once logged in let them subscribe.

00:08:09.554 --> 00:08:11.517
One thing to consider here.

00:08:11.518 --> 00:08:13.735
Such checking login function

00:08:14.177 --> 00:08:17.688
may be needed in other functions besides subscribing.

00:08:18.281 --> 00:08:23.827
For example, in the previously mentioned
chatting function may need a login, too.

00:08:27.121 --> 00:08:32.587
If you create the login logic within the subscribe action layer,

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:36.235
you can't reuse the login function in other action layer.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:41.066
It may create an overlapping code to use the same logic.

00:08:42.928 --> 00:08:45.162
In order to prevent this,

00:08:45.163 --> 00:08:48.427
we separated another layer for business logic.

00:08:49.646 --> 00:08:50.875
This is called a service layer.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.107
The service layer is separated into

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:57.094
the logic related to the actual subscription,
and the logic related to login.

00:08:57.481 --> 00:09:00.310
In such a service, logic such as "interested" might be preferred.

00:09:04.401 --> 00:09:06.980
In reality, the service layer abide to the following principles.

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:11.562
A service logic must fulfill only one function or

00:09:12.316 --> 00:09:13.688
handle unsynchronized logic,

00:09:14.057 --> 00:09:16.472
or update the discharged state.

00:09:18.378 --> 00:09:21.235
Now the part where you have to implement all these service logic is

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.475
the action layer I mentioned earlier.

00:09:24.681 --> 00:09:27.578
Using such declared service layers, in the actin layer,

00:09:28.165 --> 00:09:31.255
you can create a complicated function

00:09:32.352 --> 00:09:35.236
using different services to use it as one function.

00:09:35.954 --> 00:09:41.399
Also, when you call the actual function in the feature component,
you can use this action layer to provide connection.

00:09:43.569 --> 00:09:47.372
In the feature component, if you only recall the declared functions in the action,

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.992
you can simultaneously use the same functions.

00:09:51.645 --> 00:09:54.764
If you want to use the same function in different UI components,

00:09:55.389 --> 00:09:58.605
you can now only recall appropriate
actions for that specific function

00:09:58.698 --> 00:10:00.903
to use the same function.

00:10:04.239 --> 00:10:07.345
Okay, let's review what we have said so far.

00:10:08.402 --> 00:10:11.255
As I said before, this is the current structure.

00:10:12.766 --> 00:10:14.902
The component receives a user action.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.123
Based on this action, the business logic is activated.

00:10:20.092 --> 00:10:22.254
Using the business logic,

00:10:22.255 --> 00:10:25.886
apply it to the store and deliver it to the component again.

00:10:26.462 --> 00:10:30.413
Now the UI will change based on whatever action we took.

00:10:32.361 --> 00:10:34.675
If you look at the component box in the middle,

00:10:34.676 --> 00:10:37.220
you can see that now there's a added layer

00:10:37.773 --> 00:10:39.774
that says "content layer content component".

00:10:40.312 --> 00:10:42.764
This layer, when we realized it

00:10:42.765 --> 00:10:45.638
If there is the feature component

00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:47.761
Functions would mix for some cases

00:10:47.762 --> 00:10:50.892
So to separate the functions we layered it once more

00:10:51.072 --> 00:10:54.532
With this layer structure out of the need

00:10:55.032 --> 00:10:57.378
We can reuse and rebuild it

00:10:57.379 --> 00:10:59.962
The project can have no overlapping codes

00:11:01.192 --> 00:11:04.803
With some change in or new component

00:11:04.804 --> 00:11:08.814
The action and service layer is in charge of the function

00:11:08.815 --> 00:11:13.422
So the function already realized can be completed only by assembly

00:11:14.582 --> 00:11:17.262
The first structural issue has been resolved

00:11:18.282 --> 00:11:20.422
The second resolution,

00:11:20.423 --> 00:11:24.402
We had a service we were providing

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.607
And that service was the only one considered

00:11:26.608 --> 00:11:30.092
So there was no proper reaction for situations

00:11:34.342 --> 00:11:37.900
The video streaming service I took as an example

00:11:37.901 --> 00:11:42.221
Let's say that we are to provide the version 2020 and 2022 separately

00:11:43.162 --> 00:11:45.950
So the product has some different function

00:11:45.951 --> 00:11:48.282
And should be provided simultaneously

00:11:49.162 --> 00:11:50.242
Previously

00:11:51.193 --> 00:11:54.015
Only one service was considered in the structure

00:11:54.016 --> 00:11:56.819
Unless the resource is delivered

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.992
It was hard to use it in the other page

00:12:01.312 --> 00:12:03.429
In fact, even with realizing it in the same resource

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:08.112
The conditional statement like if is always included to respond to the domain spec

00:12:09.112 --> 00:12:12.377
In order to react to these requests with each service

00:12:12.378 --> 00:12:15.941
As the service increases, the maintenance points do

00:12:15.942 --> 00:12:18.212
And the complication of the inner logic increases

00:12:18.822 --> 00:12:21.422
It's hard to grasp the spec at once

00:12:24.032 --> 00:12:27.572
So how could we provide various services at the same time?

00:12:32.322 --> 00:12:34.528
Before resolving this issue

00:12:34.529 --> 00:12:36.922
We had to consider the following points:

00:12:37.262 --> 00:12:42.342
Now we had to react to different needs with the service

00:12:43.172 --> 00:12:45.822
We had to remove the reliance on a specific service

00:12:46.662 --> 00:12:50.121
We needed a structure to provide to various services easily

00:12:52.202 --> 00:12:56.262
To satisfy these points, we decide to modularize the product

00:12:58.232 --> 00:13:01.331
To a moduled product, we used config values

00:13:01.332 --> 00:13:02.906
The use, whether it's used

00:13:03.379 --> 00:13:06.182
We defined those customized values

00:13:06.842 --> 00:13:09.542
Config is provided for the parts that need customization

00:13:09.543 --> 00:13:11.954
And to respond to the needs

00:13:11.955 --> 00:13:15.942
We enabled the feature flag setting on the functional aspect

00:13:16.482 --> 00:13:19.925
Additionally, for it to work in different uses and situations

00:13:19.926 --> 00:13:23.130
Handler-type config is also provided

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:27.657
Like this, something I mentioned earlier

00:13:27.658 --> 00:13:32.250
JSConf Korea 2020 and 2022 logo

00:13:32.251 --> 00:13:35.510
We can adjust the config like this according to the need

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:40.200
Also with feature flag, we can decide on the aspect to use

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:45.565
In ver 2020, the subscription button is only enabled in this declaration

00:13:45.693 --> 00:13:49.069
And in ver 2022, title and profile areas are used

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:51.940
And the subscription button, not used.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:14:00.119
Inside the module, we make HOC based on the feature flag in the config

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.480
To control the use of component

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:05.052
Then, only with the feature flag

00:14:05.053 --> 00:14:09.770
The component can control whether that component should be used or not

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:14.043
With the provided options that can be customized

00:14:14.044 --> 00:14:16.960
The module can be adjusted to that service

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.510
For instance, in the 2020 version I mentioned

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:25.770
Text

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.259
And logo color is customized

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.370
And subscription button is the only enabled function

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.421
In 2020 version

00:14:32.422 --> 00:14:36.490
The logo is changed, the title and profile can be used

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:41.300
With one module, we can respond to various services

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.144
To provide these functions easily

00:14:45.145 --> 00:14:49.090
We provide a maintenance tool separately

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:53.818
So from within the module, the config value set in the admin tool

00:14:53.819 --> 00:14:56.999
It's brought in through a server communication

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:03.489
With this enabled active fetching

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:05.235
When there is an issue

00:15:05.236 --> 00:15:08.440
We can turn off the feature flag right away

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.973
Even with the new function added

00:15:11.974 --> 00:15:16.740
We can publish it first without considering the order of publication

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:23.923
In fact, according to the places to supply the service to,

00:15:23.924 --> 00:15:26.256
The options to be provided are adjusted

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:31.177
We provide it from within the internal service

00:15:31.178 --> 00:15:35.984
So we provide the service using the internal publication module

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:43.836
Including the flow and module structure

00:15:43.837 --> 00:15:46.960
Let me sum up on the overall structure

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:52.365
The overall project

00:15:52.366 --> 00:15:55.408
In fact, we provide more than one domain

00:15:55.409 --> 00:15:57.030
So it's a monorepo

00:15:57.290 --> 00:16:00.094
The aspects commonly used in each page

00:16:00.484 --> 00:16:02.539
There's the collective shared area

00:16:03.259 --> 00:16:07.046
In the area are the UI that can be shared in various domains,

00:16:07.047 --> 00:16:09.719
Business logic, or components

00:16:11.679 --> 00:16:16.117
Using them, the function for each domain is combined for configuring the page

00:16:17.519 --> 00:16:18.431
That's how it's provided

00:16:18.432 --> 00:16:23.039
Now, the view area is provided in a module format like this

00:16:26.333 --> 00:16:30.473
Could this structure improvement improve the work-life balance?

00:16:30.474 --> 00:16:33.259
Here is the review

00:16:34.789 --> 00:16:39.369
It's the prototype result with our actual project

00:16:40.399 --> 00:16:43.379
Producing a whole different layout page

00:16:44.079 --> 00:16:46.159
Didn't take a day

00:16:48.069 --> 00:16:52.213
And like this, the various needs from various services

00:16:52.214 --> 00:16:55.098
Could be responded only with the setup values

00:16:55.906 --> 00:16:59.239
Now we needed to fear no more with more services

00:17:04.288 --> 00:17:06.916
Considering this extensible design

00:17:06.917 --> 00:17:08.588
Even with new work,

00:17:08.589 --> 00:17:12.488
You can reuse the existing logic to increase productivity

00:17:12.489 --> 00:17:15.859
It decreases overlapping codes to prevent human errors

00:17:15.861 --> 00:17:18.579
And you can only focus on the functions you can actually realize

00:17:20.089 --> 00:17:24.319
And even with needing separate pages, you can now flexibly react to it

00:17:25.878 --> 00:17:29.319
So the structure improved much more from before

00:17:31.299 --> 00:17:34.845
The next wordcloud is something I gathered out of

00:17:34.846 --> 00:17:38.629
The impressions our team had with the change

00:17:39.319 --> 00:17:41.065
For our team

00:17:41.066 --> 00:17:44.530
The UI and Script developers are separate

00:17:45.109 --> 00:17:48.225
So separating UI and the logic

00:17:48.226 --> 00:17:52.344
The UI developing work got much more convenient

00:17:52.345 --> 00:17:54.959
You can see that over here

00:17:56.189 --> 00:17:59.521
Like this, to design according to the project early on

00:17:59.522 --> 00:18:01.969
You need to spend a lot of time designing

00:18:02.777 --> 00:18:05.919
But as time passes, this design shines more and more

00:18:07.969 --> 00:18:12.525
Without thinking about this in project configuration, it may be fast in the beginning

00:18:12.964 --> 00:18:15.979
But as the service grows and more situations occur

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:18.729
You'll have to spend more time in maintenance and modification

00:18:19.579 --> 00:18:23.589
We had the same situation, which made us improve the structure like this

00:18:25.479 --> 00:18:28.738
I don't mean to say spend as much time as possible in design

00:18:28.739 --> 00:18:33.739
But I am sure thinking about this will definitely help you

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:42.549
I talked about the comments and experienced benefits my coworkers and I had

00:18:43.059 --> 00:18:46.389
The keyword for today I intended was work-life balance

00:18:47.404 --> 00:18:48.409
How was it?

00:18:51.432 --> 00:18:52.422
Thank you

00:18:53.183 --> 00:18:57.003
In my opinion, by separating the UI and functions

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.921
The reusability improved

00:18:58.922 --> 00:19:01.282
With the on-off function enabled

00:19:01.283 --> 00:19:03.789
We could respond as a platform as well

00:19:05.629 --> 00:19:07.569
Now, even with the same request

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:11.329
We can respond much faster compared to the previous structure

00:19:13.445 --> 00:19:16.543
Our project, as I was preparing for this presentation

00:19:16.544 --> 00:19:20.810
Went through so many structure and capacity improvement as well

00:19:21.069 --> 00:19:24.449
It's a shame I can't share everything today

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:29.784
There are points on better design or capacity too

00:19:29.785 --> 00:19:32.117
If you visit me later, let's talk about it together

00:19:32.118 --> 00:19:36.049
I think I should replace it with that

00:19:36.229 --> 00:19:42.249
And the shared design method today isn't the ultimate answer

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:47.094
For each project, there may be different design that fits

00:19:47.095 --> 00:19:51.749
For a small project, this big layering structure ay actually harm you

00:19:52.794 --> 00:19:59.189
Likewise, the design for each service and improve through discussion

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:02.769
Since our team provides a big service

00:20:02.969 --> 00:20:04.989
The layering for that big service

00:20:05.429 --> 00:20:08.489
Is what I experienced and shared here

00:20:10.649 --> 00:20:13.763
If, not only our project

00:20:13.764 --> 00:20:16.628
But also various projects begin this design thinking

00:20:16.629 --> 00:20:20.238
I'm sure it will contribute to the development of the JavaScript world

00:20:23.217 --> 00:20:27.999
That's it for today's presentation with the extensible design as the theme

00:20:28.309 --> 00:20:30.389
If you had similar concerns

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:33.399
Or if you'd like to have such concerns

00:20:33.779 --> 00:20:36.772
Or if you want to give me another insight

00:20:36.773 --> 00:20:40.679
Please come talk to me, you're very welcomed to do so

00:20:40.859 --> 00:20:42.199
Thank you

